$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2.2 General Procedure for the Reduction of
Nitroarenes The reduction of 4-nitrophenol (4-NP) by NaBH4 was chosen as
a model reaction to investigate the catalytic performance of the prepared
Pd/g-C3N4 catalyst. Generally, 2.9 mL water and 100 μL 4-NP (0.01 M) were
added to a 3.5 mL colorimetric ware, followed by adding 25 μL freshly
prepared NaBH4 solution (0.5 M). After that, 5 μL Pd/g-C3N4 catalyst (5
mg mL-1) was added to the above mixed solution. The reaction process was
monitored by ultraviolet visible spectra (UV-Vis). Entry: 3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
