$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-(3,5-Dimethoxyphenyl)-2-methylpropan-1-ol (13). To a solution of 12
(1.70 g, 8.16 mmol) in anhydrous methanol (40 mL) at room temperature
under an argon atmosphere was added sodium borohydride (1.39 g, 36.7
mmol) portionwise. The reaction mixture was stirred for 1 h and then
quenched by the addition of aqueous 1 N HCl and extracted with ethyl
acetate. The organic layer was washed with brine, dried (MgSO4), and
evaporated. Purification by flash column chromatograph on silica gel (20%
ethyl acetate in hexane). 13 (1.6 g, 94%) as a colorless oil. IR (neat):
3433 (br, OH), 2961, 2836, 1592, 1456, 1422, 1202, 1159, 1048 cm-1. 1H
NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.53 (d, J = 2.0 Hz, 2H, ArH), 6.34 (t, J = 2.0
Hz, 1H, ArH), 3.80 (s, 6H, -OCH3), 3.58 (s, 2H, -CH2OH), 1.30 (s, 6H,
-C(CH3)2-). Mass spectrum (ESI) m/z (relative intensity) 211 (M+ + H,
100).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
